Sample SQL Queries
Student, Room and Hostel Details
SELECT
    s.Name,
    r.Room_Number,
    h.Hostel_Name
FROM student s
JOIN allocation a
    ON s.Student_ID = a.Student_ID
JOIN room r
    ON a.Room_ID = r.Room_ID
JOIN hostel h
    ON r.Hostel_ID = h.Hostel_ID;

Aggregate Query
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS Total_Students,
    SUM(Amount) AS Total_Payment,
    AVG(Amount) AS Average_Payment
FROM payment;

Available Rooms
SELECT *
FROM room
WHERE Status = 'Available';

Pending Complaints
SELECT *
FROM complaint
WHERE Status = 'Pending';

Hostel-wise Student Count
SELECT
    h.Hostel_Name,
    COUNT(a.Student_ID) AS Total_Students
FROM hostel h
JOIN room r
    ON h.Hostel_ID = r.Hostel_ID
JOIN allocation a
    ON r.Room_ID = a.Room_ID
GROUP BY h.Hostel_ID, h.Hostel_Name;

How to Run the Project
1. Clone the Repository
git clone <GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL>

2. Open the Project
cd DBMS-Course-Project

3. Install Dependencies
npm install

4. Create the MySQL Database
Open MySQL and execute:
CREATE DATABASE hostelmanagement;

Select the database:
USE hostelmanagement;

Then execute the SQL file:
database/hostelmanagement.sql

This creates the required tables and sample records.
5. Configure MySQL Connection
Open:
backend/db.js

Update the MySQL credentials:
const db = mysql.createConnection({
    host: "localhost",
    user: "root",
    password: "YOUR_MYSQL_PASSWORD",
    database: "hostelmanagement",
    port: 3306
});

Replace YOUR_MYSQL_PASSWORD with your local MySQL password.
6. Start the Backend
Run:
node backend/server.js

The server will run at:
http://localhost:3000

7. Open the Application
Open the frontend in your browser using the configured application route.
